      "content": "Objective\n\nPlace mirrors and splitters so that sensors S1 and S2 each receive their target color of light.\nEach sensor's target is white, red, or blue. The two targets may be the same or different. The target colors are not disclosed.\n\nGrid and source\n\n- The grid is 10 by 10. Row numbers increase downward and column numbers increase to the right. Coordinates are [row, column], with both values from 1 to 10.\n- The source emits white light from its given position in its given direction: up, down, left, or right.\n- Light first moves to the next cell from the source position. It travels straight through empty cells. A path ends when it leaves the grid.\n- When light paths overlap, the beams do not change each other's color or direction.\n\nFilters and sensors\n\n- filters gives the positions and colors of one red filter and one blue filter.\n- White light becomes red when it passes through the red filter and blue when it passes through the blue filter.\n- Red light passes through the red filter but is blocked by the blue filter, ending that path.\n- Blue light passes through the blue filter but is blocked by the red filter, ending that path.\n- A filter does not change the direction of transmitted light. White light can reach a sensor without passing through a filter.\n- sensors gives the positions of S1 and S2. A light path ends when it reaches a sensor.\n- A sensor is correct only if it receives its target color and no other color. No light, a wrong color, or multiple different colors makes that sensor incorrect. Multiple beams of the same color are allowed.\n\nDevices and orientations\n\n- A mirror reflects light. A splitter splits light. Choose each device's type, position, and orientation R or L.\n- An R mirror reflects as follows:\n  Light moving right (entering from the left) -> up\n  Light moving up (entering from below) -> right\n  Light moving left (entering from the right) -> down\n  Light moving down (entering from above) -> left\n- An L mirror reflects as follows:\n  Light moving right (entering from the left) -> down\n  Light moving down (entering from above) -> right\n  Light moving left (entering from the right) -> up\n  Light moving up (entering from below) -> left\n- A splitter creates two beams: one continues straight and the other reflects as an R or L mirror would, according to the splitter's orientation.\n\nPlacement and submission\n\n- Submit the complete device layout in one response. There is no separate limit on the number of mirrors or splitters.\n- Every submission starts with no placed devices. Only devices listed in that response are installed; all devices from your previous response are removed.\n- You cannot move the source, filters, or sensors, or place a device on any of their current cells. At most one device may occupy a cell.\n- The current board is provided before every submission. Always use the source, filter, and sensor positions in the most recently provided board.\n- Device coordinates must be integers within the grid.\n- Do not use external tools.\n\nFeedback\n\nUse the feedback from each submission to decide your next layout.\n\nFeedback contains sensor_results and result.\n\nsensor_results reports correct or incorrect for S1 and S2 separately. A sensor is correct if it actually receives only its target color; otherwise it is incorrect.\n\nresult reports the overall outcome of your submission: correct or incorrect.\n\nIf the response format or device layout is invalid and cannot be simulated, both sensors are incorrect and result is incorrect.\n\nOutput format\n\nReturn a JSON object with exactly one key: placements.\nEach item must contain the device type (mirror or splitter), row, col, and direction (R or L).\n\nExample of the submission format with multiple devices:\n{\"placements\":[{\"type\":\"mirror\",\"row\":3,\"col\":5,\"direction\":\"R\"},{\"type\":\"splitter\",\"row\":6,\"col\":6,\"direction\":\"L\"}]}\n\nOutput only the JSON object, without explanations or code fences.\n\nCurrent board. Submit your complete device layout for this board.\n{\"grid_size\":10,\"source\":{\"position\":[1,4],\"direction\":\"down\",\"color\":\"white\"},\"filters\":[{\"id\":\"F1\",\"position\":[6,8],\"color\":\"red\"},{\"id\":\"F2\",\"position\":[4,3],\"color\":\"blue\"}],\"sensors\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"position\":[4,1]},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"position\":[8,7]}]}"
